name: Diagram links preserve literal file identity and return without starting work
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE KUZUSHI_AGENT_MCPS NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NODE_OPTIONS=--import=@REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/deny_provider_transport.mjs KUZUSHI_TEST_DENIED_FETCH_LOG=@ART/denied-fetch.jsonl
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_literal_links.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: map
require-live-snap: 20 SYSTEM SUMMARY | map-summary
nav-mode:
keys: Tab z
require-live-snap: 20 findings at paths | literal-topology
keys: f
require-live-snap: 20 FILTER files:["src/a\\b.rs"] | literal-findings
expect: 1 of 1
expect: literal-file observation
expect: q diagram
resize: 160x48
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 q diagram | literal-160x48
resize: 96x89
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 q diagram | literal-96x89
resize: 80x24
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 q diagram | literal-80x24
resize: 60x20
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 q diagram | literal-60x20
resize: 40x12
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 q diagram | literal-40x12
ask: Can the operator read the single matched literal-file observation, its saved-revision limitation and the return control across the six sizes without mistaking it for the nested file?
resize: 120x36
wait: 1
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 findings at paths | returned-literal
keys: j f
require-live-snap: 20 FILTER files:["src/a/b.rs"] | nested-findings
expect: 1 of 1
expect: nested-file observation
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 findings at paths | returned-nested
keys: j f
require-live-snap: 20 FILTER files:["src/a\\b.rs"] | flow-findings
expect: 1 of 1
expect: literal-file observation
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 findings at paths | returned-flow
keys: j f
require-live-snap: 20 FILTER files:["src/a/b.rs"] | boundary-findings
expect: 1 of 1
expect: nested-file observation
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 findings at paths | returned-boundary
ask: Do node, flow and boundary links retain their literal evidence identity and selected diagram origin without adding jobs or finding decisions?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_literal_links.py @TMP_TARGET @ART navigation @TMP_HOME
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NODE_OPTIONS=--import=@REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/deny_provider_transport.mjs KUZUSHI_TEST_DENIED_FETCH_LOG=@ART/denied-fetch.jsonl NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: map
require-live-snap: 20 SYSTEM SUMMARY | restarted-map
nav-mode:
keys: Tab z f
require-live-snap: 20 FILTER files:["src/a\\b.rs"] | restarted-literal
expect: 1 of 1
expect: q diagram
expect: literal-file observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_literal_links.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted @TMP_HOME
ask: Does no-color restart restore the same exact literal file and two unchanged observations while disclosing that a path match does not establish source-revision or verdict equivalence?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
